{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \u201cMr. Jay, is the government running with the fox and chasing with the hounds?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked: \u201cBut why shouldn't it be a suit contesting the constitutionality? \u2026 what is the point of going through any kind of administrative process of the refund route?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked: \u201cNothing different from what it is now, but just Congress makes clear that a tax and alleged violation of the Export Clause falls within the term \u2018any Internal Revenue tax\u2019?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \u201cWhy is the Export Clause so, so significant? The only other self\u2011executing constitutional clause that provides for damages automatically that comes to mind is the Takings Clause.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked: \u201cPlus you get interest.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked: \u201cIs the interest the same in amount in either case?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked: \u201cBUT \u2014 the use of any Internal Revenue tax, and your whole argument is this isn\u2019t an Internal Revenue tax.\u201d"
      }
    ],
