  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (William M. Jay)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (William M. Jay), the United States argues that the case falls under Title\u202f26 tax\u2011refund provisions, asserting that the respondents have already received the full tax refund and interest."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (William M. Jay)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (William M. Jay), the United States further contends that because the respondents cannot proceed under the exclusive tax\u2011refund procedure, they cannot plead constitutional damages instead."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents (Patricia A. Millett)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondents (Patricia A. Millett), clintwood Elkhorn Mining Co. argues that the government must assert a plausible basis for tax liability to invoke the tax\u2011refund scheme, and that the government has not done so."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Millett, clintwood Elkhorn Mining Co. maintains that any tax is one that the government asserts as valid; it need not be correct, only asserted."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Clintwood Elkhorn Mining Co. points out that there is no administrative avenue such as tax court for this particular tax."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Jay, the United States asserts that the tax on coal mined in the United States is facially constitutional."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Millett, clintwood Elkhorn Mining Co. argues that a claimant need only show an overpayment, not that they went through the administrative scheme."
      }
    ],
